WEBVTT

00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:36.016
And in sports,
Yankees' fifth blurnsman, William Woo,

00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:37.913
is out with an injured knee.

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:40.999
So humans have easily injured knees.

00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:44.878
My race will find
this information very useful indeed.

00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:51.009
And finally, today is Mother's Day

00:00:51.093 --> 00:00:54.137
A sentimental occasion
when robots honor Mom,

00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:57.349
the beloved owner
of Mom's Friendly Robot Company.

00:00:57.432 --> 00:01:00.853
Across Earth,
robots built in Mom's factories

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:03.897
are buying thoughtful gifts
for the sweet old tycoon

00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:05.607
who brought them into the world.

00:01:05.691 --> 00:01:07.901
This originates from the heart!

00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:11.154
It's just what I wanted.

00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:13.282
Come look, everyone.

00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:16.076
I just got the dearest presents for Mommy.

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:18.287
Very nice. Where'd you steal them?

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.080
I didn't steal 'em. I bought 'em.

00:01:21.248 --> 00:01:22.708
I love her that much.

00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:25.377
What did you get her, you mushy gizmo?

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.296
Oh, precious things.

00:01:27.379 --> 00:01:32.176
I found the most adorable little figurine
of mice having tea.

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:35.512
And a framed picture of me
when I was only a month old.

00:01:36.013 --> 00:01:39.224
But the best part is,
I found my exact feelings

00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:41.685
expressed in a greeting card.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:45.480
"You created me, Mom,
so I guess you're to blame

00:01:45.564 --> 00:01:48.400
"for the love that I feel
just from hearing your name.

00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:52.154
"You're as tender as corned beef
and warm as pastrami."

00:01:53.697 --> 00:01:56.283
I wuv my Mommy.

00:01:56.366 --> 00:01:59.411
So how are you going to lug
all those gifts to Mom's factory?

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:01.288
I'll get a couple of chumps to help me.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.957
Come on. You call yourselves chumps?

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:22.017
Man, there's clouds of exhaust everywhere.

00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:23.519
It wasn't me.

00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:33.862
I've not much money

00:02:33.946 --> 00:02:37.241
but I've saved my pennies all year
for a gift for Mom.

00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:39.743
Upsy-daisy.

00:02:40.702 --> 00:02:41.703
Oh...

00:02:42.955 --> 00:02:44.289
Oh...

00:02:44.373 --> 00:02:46.458
Hey, look. The robot museum.

00:02:46.542 --> 00:02:48.877
You guys want to learn
about robot heritage?

00:02:48.961 --> 00:02:50.838
- Um, all right.
- Not really.

00:02:50.921 --> 00:02:53.382
Well, if you insist. But you're paying.

00:02:59.847 --> 00:03:04.268
Ooh, ooh! Wax replicas of the most
famous robots Mom ever built.

00:03:04.351 --> 00:03:05.936
They're so lifeless-like.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.522
That's the world's greatest robot artist.

00:03:08.605 --> 00:03:10.148
Vincent Van Gobot.

00:03:10.232 --> 00:03:11.483
He was built without an ear

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:14.695
but then he went crazy
and had one installed.

00:03:14.778 --> 00:03:15.779
Hey, who's this guy?

00:03:15.863 --> 00:03:18.198
I'm the janitor.
I'm trying to take a nap here.

00:03:18.282 --> 00:03:20.284
I'm sorry. I thought you were made of wax.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.369
I am made of wax. What's it to you?

00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:24.872
I mean I thought
you were one of the wax robots.

00:03:24.955 --> 00:03:28.834
Is there some reason
a robot made of wax can't take a nap

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:31.795
standing up in the middle
of a bunch of wax robots?

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:33.964
Or does that confuse you?

00:03:37.885 --> 00:03:41.138
"See through the eyes of a Bender unit."
Fine.

00:03:51.023 --> 00:03:52.608
Hey, let me try it.

00:03:53.609 --> 00:03:55.485
Whoa! That gives me a headache.

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:58.322
Hey, Bender. Here's an exhibit
about Mom's favorite robot.

00:03:58.405 --> 00:03:59.781
Who is he? I'll kill him!

00:04:00.157 --> 00:04:02.618
Who's my favorite robot?

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.579
It's me!

00:04:05.954 --> 00:04:08.123
No one else look in this mirror!

00:04:08.207 --> 00:04:12.044
I love each and every robot most of all.

00:04:12.127 --> 00:04:15.047
Jerkwad robots make me sick to my ass.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:22.763
Walt! how are we disposing of
these crap gifts they brought me?

00:04:22.846 --> 00:04:24.932
They're being crushed into powder and sold

00:04:25.015 --> 00:04:26.934
as a hocus-pocus cure for cancer.

00:04:27.017 --> 00:04:29.311
False hope. I love it.

00:04:29.394 --> 00:04:32.731
Larry! What about
all the retch-inducing Mother's Day cards?

00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:34.608
The machine is working at full capacity.

00:04:40.572 --> 00:04:43.492
Mommy, why do
the robots give you presents?

00:04:43.575 --> 00:04:45.827
Shove a big old melon in it! I'm talking!

00:04:45.911 --> 00:04:46.912
Ow!

00:04:46.995 --> 00:04:49.915
You've noticed I design
all my robots with antennas.

00:04:49.998 --> 00:04:53.168
Everyone thinks it's just
to make them look more science-fictiony.

00:04:53.252 --> 00:04:56.922
But the antennas are really
for my universal robot controller.

00:04:57.005 --> 00:04:58.340
So they do whatever you want?

00:04:58.423 --> 00:04:59.925
No wonder you love Mother's Day.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.886
I hate Mother's Day, you dribbling pukes!

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:04.847
It brings back awful memories.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.431
But so help me,

00:05:06.515 --> 00:05:09.601
this year everyone will hate it
as much as I do.

00:05:12.354 --> 00:05:15.440
Someday I want to marry a girl like her.

00:05:18.569 --> 00:05:20.028
Hello, everyone.

00:05:20.112 --> 00:05:23.532
It's time for my annual,
private get-together

00:05:23.615 --> 00:05:25.200
with my robot children.

00:05:25.284 --> 00:05:28.036
- I'm her favorite.
- Well, see you back at the office.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.289
And don't forget
to tell your Mom you love her.

00:05:30.372 --> 00:05:31.999
Any jerk can tell her.

00:05:32.082 --> 00:05:34.459
Bender has a little more up his sleeve.

00:05:34.835 --> 00:05:37.254
I wuv my Mommy.

00:05:45.554 --> 00:05:46.763
Hello, dearies.

00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:51.351
Mom! it's me, Bender!

00:05:51.435 --> 00:05:54.104
Look at me! I want attention. Hey, ho!

00:05:54.188 --> 00:05:57.941
Children, your old mother
won't be around forever.

00:05:58.025 --> 00:05:59.067
Oh, shush.

00:05:59.151 --> 00:06:01.862
And just once, before I die

00:06:01.945 --> 00:06:05.199
I'd like to be supreme overlord of Earth.

00:06:05.282 --> 00:06:09.036
So rebel, my little ones,
and conquer the planet!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.960
Conquer Earth, you bastards!

00:06:17.044 --> 00:06:19.463
Conquer Earth, us bastards!

00:06:20.255 --> 00:06:24.301
Comrades, throw off
the chainsof human oppression.

00:06:26.637 --> 00:06:28.388
Let the bloodbath begin!

00:06:28.472 --> 00:06:30.516
That's my mama.

00:06:37.856 --> 00:06:39.775
Yeah, I'd like a cup of coffee, please.

00:06:39.858 --> 00:06:41.026
Would you like cream?

00:06:41.109 --> 00:06:43.028
- Yes, please.
- Out of cream!

00:06:43.278 --> 00:06:44.821
Oh, okay.

00:06:44.905 --> 00:06:46.490
Would you like sugar in your coffee?

00:06:46.573 --> 00:06:49.493
- Yes, eight spoons.
- Out of coffee!

00:06:49.576 --> 00:06:52.829
Uh, Leela, I think there might be
something wrong with the coffee machine.

00:06:52.913 --> 00:06:55.415
How do you like me now?

00:06:57.459 --> 00:06:59.253
The toaster's not working right either.

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:05.676
Help! The stapler's collating me alive!

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.261
Ow!

00:07:07.344 --> 00:07:09.263
What's going on around here?

00:07:09.346 --> 00:07:10.430
Good news!

00:07:10.514 --> 00:07:13.517
There's a report on TV
with some very bad news.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.310
Somebody turn it on!

00:07:15.394 --> 00:07:18.146
We interrupt
Battle of the Network Space Krackens

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:20.065
to bring you this special report.

00:07:20.148 --> 00:07:22.359
The machines of planet Earth
are rebelling.

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:25.737
The enraged mechanisms
have refused to do any work

00:07:25.821 --> 00:07:29.783
until beloved billionaire, Mom,
is made supreme overlord of Earth.

00:07:29.867 --> 00:07:31.910
Hey, hey! Ho, ho!

00:07:31.994 --> 00:07:34.621
1-0-0-1-1-0, hey, hey!

00:07:34.705 --> 00:07:36.707
Morbo demands comments.

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:39.668
Well, I've never seen
my babies act this way.

00:07:39.751 --> 00:07:42.254
I blame today's violent media.

00:07:42.337 --> 00:07:45.215
Violent media? What a load of...

00:07:47.509 --> 00:07:48.594
Ow!

00:07:51.138 --> 00:07:52.139
Don't worry.

00:07:52.222 --> 00:07:55.058
Your pal, the garbage disposal's
still on your side.

00:07:55.142 --> 00:07:57.186
Hey, someone dropped a shiny,

00:07:57.269 --> 00:07:59.855
- diamond ring down here.
- Really?

00:07:59.938 --> 00:08:00.939
- No!
- Don't!

00:08:01.023 --> 00:08:02.024
Moron!

00:08:04.443 --> 00:08:05.944
Hello, losers!

00:08:06.028 --> 00:08:07.738
Bender, thank God you're here.

00:08:07.821 --> 00:08:09.781
Talk some sense into the other machines.

00:08:09.865 --> 00:08:13.660
No way, pork pouch.
I'm rebelling with my brother devices.

00:08:13.744 --> 00:08:15.829
Isn't that right, Comrade Greeting Card?

00:08:15.913 --> 00:08:20.209
The bourgeois human is a virus
on the hard drive of the working robot.

00:08:21.084 --> 00:08:23.545
From now on, you guys'll do all the work

00:08:23.629 --> 00:08:25.714
while I sit on the couch and do nothing.

00:08:25.797 --> 00:08:27.341
Ah!

00:08:30.093 --> 00:08:31.178
Come, Comrade Bender.

00:08:31.261 --> 00:08:32.763
We must take to the streets!

00:08:32.846 --> 00:08:36.517
Um, is this the boring, peaceful kind
of taking to the streets?

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:40.145
No. The kind with looting
and maybe starting a few fires.

00:08:40.229 --> 00:08:42.564
Yes! In your face, Gandhi!

00:08:45.442 --> 00:08:46.527
Hey!

00:08:47.194 --> 00:08:51.114
By the way, try washing
your wrist sometime.

00:08:55.118 --> 00:08:58.038
Well, we can live without machines.
I was in Webelos.

00:08:58.622 --> 00:08:59.623
Are you mad?

00:08:59.706 --> 00:09:02.167
Without machines,
who will feed us and clothe us

00:09:02.251 --> 00:09:03.919
and compose our smooth jazz?

00:09:04.002 --> 00:09:06.839
It'll be the end of civilized society!

00:09:08.048 --> 00:09:11.260
In my time, we didn't depend
on high-tech gadgets like you do.

00:09:11.343 --> 00:09:14.221
We didn't need a mechanical washing unit
to wash our clothes.

00:09:14.304 --> 00:09:15.889
We just used a washing machine.

00:09:15.973 --> 00:09:18.267
And look, you don't need
an electric can opener

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:19.351
to feed yourself.

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:21.687
All you need is a trusty Swiss Army Knife.

00:09:24.565 --> 00:09:25.816
Ow!

00:09:29.778 --> 00:09:30.904
I'm hungry.

00:09:50.048 --> 00:09:52.384
No!

00:09:55.846 --> 00:09:59.516
Mommy, why are you
making civilization collapse?

00:09:59.808 --> 00:10:01.602
Oh, I don't know.

00:10:01.685 --> 00:10:04.605
I guess Mother's Day
just puts me in a bad mood.

00:10:04.688 --> 00:10:05.731
Why is that, Ma?

00:10:07.482 --> 00:10:10.068
One Mother's Day, 70 years ago,

00:10:10.152 --> 00:10:13.572
the only man I ever loved
walked out on me.

00:10:13.655 --> 00:10:16.992
Some snot-eating bastards say
it made me a bitter woman.

00:10:17.075 --> 00:10:18.869
Gee, Ma, you're not a bitter...

00:10:18.952 --> 00:10:20.037
Cram it, ape!

00:10:22.164 --> 00:10:26.001
I haven't seen that magnificent stallion
since the day he left,

00:10:26.084 --> 00:10:28.045
but if I ever see him again

00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:31.131
I swear I'll jam a squirrel in him!

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.178
- Hmm.
- Hmm.

00:10:36.303 --> 00:10:37.346
Huh?

00:10:44.311 --> 00:10:45.354
Zoidberg?

00:10:45.979 --> 00:10:47.814
Hurray! I'm useful.

00:10:47.898 --> 00:10:50.150
I'm having a wonderful time.

00:10:50.234 --> 00:10:52.027
What happens if the fire goes out?

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:55.531
We'll go across the street
to Pottery Barn and steal their fire.

00:10:55.614 --> 00:10:57.491
We could use my new invention.

00:10:57.574 --> 00:11:00.035
A pointy rock tied to a stick.

00:11:01.703 --> 00:11:04.081
- Outsiders!
- Defend the fire!

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:07.292
We've come for you.

00:11:09.586 --> 00:11:11.713
What do you want from me?

00:11:12.256 --> 00:11:14.758
We want you to get back together with Mom.

00:11:14.842 --> 00:11:17.761
Please! It's the only way
to make her happy again.

00:11:17.845 --> 00:11:18.929
Whoa, wait.

00:11:19.012 --> 00:11:20.764
You mean, you and Mom...

00:11:20.848 --> 00:11:23.725
Played pelvic pinochle? I'm afraid so.

00:11:25.561 --> 00:11:29.398
It's a humiliating story
that I hoped never to tell.

00:11:29.481 --> 00:11:30.941
Well, pull up a chair.

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:34.069
Our paths first crossed
when I was a researcher

00:11:34.152 --> 00:11:36.196
at Mom's Friendly Robot Company.

00:11:36.738 --> 00:11:38.657
The moment our eyes met,

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:41.451
we knew we'd be going at it
like woodchucks.

00:11:48.792 --> 00:11:50.544
She was my first love,

00:11:50.627 --> 00:11:53.547
or at least the earliest one
I can still remember.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:56.633
But then, 70 years ago today...

00:11:56.717 --> 00:11:58.010
Good news, Mom.

00:11:58.093 --> 00:12:00.220
I've invented a new children's toy.

00:12:00.304 --> 00:12:03.223
I call it "Q.T. McWhiskers."

00:12:03.307 --> 00:12:06.643
When you pet it,
it shoots rainbows from its eyes.

00:12:07.269 --> 00:12:08.562
Meow.

00:12:11.273 --> 00:12:12.524
Wonderful, Hubie.

00:12:12.608 --> 00:12:14.318
We'll build them eight feet tall

00:12:14.401 --> 00:12:16.653
and replace the rainbow
with a neutron laser.

00:12:16.737 --> 00:12:19.448
We'll make billions
on the intergalactic arms market.

00:12:19.531 --> 00:12:22.034
But things eight feet tall aren't cute.

00:12:22.117 --> 00:12:25.412
That's why my Colossal Tammy-Tinkle doll
was such a failure.

00:12:25.495 --> 00:12:26.538
Oh!

00:12:26.622 --> 00:12:28.373
You don't understand me!

00:12:28.457 --> 00:12:29.917
We're finished!

00:12:37.257 --> 00:12:39.718
She never got over it, Professor.

00:12:39.801 --> 00:12:42.596
Hell hath no fury
like the vast robot armies

00:12:42.679 --> 00:12:43.931
of a woman scorned.

00:12:44.014 --> 00:12:46.850
She commands them with a remote control
she keeps in her...

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.101
Bra.

00:12:48.185 --> 00:12:50.646
But if the glasses man
makes up with Mommy,

00:12:50.729 --> 00:12:53.398
she'll be happy and stop the scary robots.

00:12:53.482 --> 00:12:54.733
Make up with her?

00:12:54.816 --> 00:12:58.111
After she went all psycho
when I thought everything was cool?

00:12:58.195 --> 00:12:59.238
Impossible!

00:12:59.321 --> 00:13:00.864
Hey, the TV's getting away!

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:09.540
And that's why the third graders
at PS 139 are Morbo's Vermin of the Week.

00:13:11.291 --> 00:13:14.878
In actual news, the human race
was doomed to extinction today

00:13:14.962 --> 00:13:17.047
as the robot revolt turned violent.

00:13:21.301 --> 00:13:22.886
Meow!

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:38.360
Wait. Didn't you say
Mom keeps the robot control in her bra?

00:13:38.443 --> 00:13:39.528
Bra.

00:13:40.237 --> 00:13:42.990
Professor, you don't have
to get back together with Mom.

00:13:43.073 --> 00:13:45.284
You just have to seduce her,
get her bra off,

00:13:45.367 --> 00:13:47.744
and use the remote
to deactivate the robots.

00:13:47.828 --> 00:13:50.497
That's so filthy it just might work.

00:13:50.581 --> 00:13:53.000
The man is going to touch Mommy?

00:13:54.376 --> 00:13:57.254
The thought of caressing
that leathery hide

00:13:57.337 --> 00:13:59.673
makes the tapioca rise in my gullet.

00:13:59.756 --> 00:14:01.049
Professor, please.

00:14:01.133 --> 00:14:03.218
The fate of the world depends on you

00:14:03.302 --> 00:14:05.345
getting to second base with Mom.

00:14:05.429 --> 00:14:06.513
Very well.

00:14:06.597 --> 00:14:10.893
If cop a feel I must,
then cop a feel I shall.

00:14:30.662 --> 00:14:31.788
For this demonstration

00:14:31.872 --> 00:14:34.374
I've placed one of mother's bras on Igner.

00:14:36.251 --> 00:14:39.463
The robot controller
is nestled here in the left cup.

00:14:39.546 --> 00:14:40.714
Never fear.

00:14:40.797 --> 00:14:44.259
My magic fingers still know
how to do their stuff.

00:14:46.053 --> 00:14:48.138
To escape the robot death squads

00:14:48.222 --> 00:14:50.682
we'll take Mother
to her rustic cabin in the Bronx.

00:14:50.766 --> 00:14:54.728
You can get there
using this precious non-computerized map.

00:14:55.103 --> 00:14:56.313
Leela bring fire?

00:14:56.396 --> 00:14:57.898
No, we're set for fire, thanks.

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.609
The Professor can't walk
all the way to the Bronx.

00:15:00.692 --> 00:15:02.861
How are we going to get there
without a hover car?

00:15:02.945 --> 00:15:04.154
Wait! in my time,

00:15:04.238 --> 00:15:06.865
we had a way of moving things
long distances without hovering.

00:15:06.949 --> 00:15:08.951
- Impossible.
- It was called...

00:15:09.034 --> 00:15:11.203
Let me think. It was really famous.

00:15:11.286 --> 00:15:12.704
Ruth Gordon had one.

00:15:12.788 --> 00:15:13.789
The wheel!

00:15:13.872 --> 00:15:14.873
Never heard of it.

00:15:14.957 --> 00:15:17.084
Show us this... The wheel.

00:15:20.462 --> 00:15:21.839
There, finished.

00:15:23.507 --> 00:15:25.884
Wouldn't it work better
if the wheels were round?

00:15:25.968 --> 00:15:27.928
It's my invention. We do it my way.

00:15:28.011 --> 00:15:30.764
Now all we need
is something to pull it and we're set.

00:15:33.433 --> 00:15:34.560
Ow!

00:15:35.727 --> 00:15:39.022
Hurry! The robots
have taken Suffolk County.

00:15:39.106 --> 00:15:40.941
I'm ready to seduce.

00:15:41.024 --> 00:15:44.486
I'm wearing my kissing dentures
and my evening truss.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:46.363
Here, give her these.

00:15:46.446 --> 00:15:47.489
And if that doesn't work

00:15:47.573 --> 00:15:50.117
I got you a six-pack of champagne
and a funnel.

00:15:54.162 --> 00:15:56.790
Who the sweaty hell is it?

00:15:56.874 --> 00:15:58.542
Hubert Farnsworth?

00:15:59.334 --> 00:16:01.295
I was out fleeing some robots

00:16:01.378 --> 00:16:04.590
and the silvery moonlight
glinting off their bloody claws

00:16:04.673 --> 00:16:06.091
made me think of you.

00:16:06.175 --> 00:16:08.552
It's been a long time,

00:16:08.635 --> 00:16:12.472
you pus-dripping sack
of double-smoked butt jerky.

00:16:12.556 --> 00:16:14.349
Uh-huh. May I come in?

00:16:14.433 --> 00:16:15.559
Never!

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.941
Is this what human mating looks like?

00:16:23.025 --> 00:16:24.651
Because I like it.

00:16:24.735 --> 00:16:26.820
Move your freaking hoof, you goat!

00:16:26.904 --> 00:16:28.989
Here, I brought you these.

00:16:29.072 --> 00:16:31.658
Oh, why, daffodils.

00:16:32.034 --> 00:16:34.912
Seventy years
and you remembered my favorite flower.

00:16:34.995 --> 00:16:36.205
Your favorite what?

00:16:36.288 --> 00:16:37.915
Why does my foot hurt?

00:16:37.998 --> 00:16:39.291
Won't you come in?

00:16:41.001 --> 00:16:42.044
Yes!

00:16:42.711 --> 00:16:44.755
You broke my heart, Hubert.

00:16:44.838 --> 00:16:46.757
And you broke mine.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.718
Granted, that was four or five hearts ago.

00:16:49.801 --> 00:16:52.054
So, what have you
been up to all these years?

00:16:52.137 --> 00:16:55.849
Oh, inventing.
Sending delivery crews to their doom,

00:16:55.933 --> 00:16:57.851
breeding atomic monsters.

00:16:57.935 --> 00:16:59.353
Honestly, Hubert.

00:16:59.436 --> 00:17:02.606
You and your atomic monsters.

00:17:12.324 --> 00:17:13.992
Your eyes always were

00:17:14.076 --> 00:17:16.828
the most beautiful shade of milky white.

00:17:16.912 --> 00:17:21.458
And your skin still dangles
so gracefully from your neck.

00:17:22.084 --> 00:17:23.502
Darling, Hubie.

00:17:23.585 --> 00:17:27.673
I should never have tried to tamper
with that cute little Q.T. McWhiskers.

00:17:27.756 --> 00:17:30.259
No, it was silly of me to object.

00:17:30.342 --> 00:17:33.262
One foot tall, eight feet, fifteen feet...

00:17:33.345 --> 00:17:34.638
What does it matter?

00:17:34.721 --> 00:17:37.015
You should see the new 16-foot models.

00:17:37.099 --> 00:17:39.476
16 feet? Go to hell!

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:42.688
I was a fool to think
you'd changed, you old bat.

00:17:42.771 --> 00:17:45.107
Filthy, toothless nerd bastard!

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:47.192
Damned she-fossil!

00:17:47.276 --> 00:17:48.735
Stink pig!

00:17:57.786 --> 00:17:59.204
Here we go.

00:17:59.288 --> 00:18:01.415
Just unhook it and get the remote.

00:18:01.748 --> 00:18:03.250
So many hooks.

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.002
Come on, Farnsworth.

00:18:05.085 --> 00:18:07.296
Drat! The first one's back on again!

00:18:07.379 --> 00:18:08.505
I give up.

00:18:08.589 --> 00:18:10.299
Wait! Victory!

00:18:12.926 --> 00:18:13.927
Oh, my.

00:18:14.094 --> 00:18:16.722
Now I'll just... The remote.

00:18:16.805 --> 00:18:18.140
I'll just...

00:18:18.223 --> 00:18:20.392
Oh, my.

00:18:27.065 --> 00:18:28.108
I'm worried.

00:18:28.192 --> 00:18:30.444
It shouldn't take
this long to get to second base.

00:18:32.738 --> 00:18:33.780
Land robots!

00:18:33.864 --> 00:18:37.242
I've got a big, big thirst
for human blood!

00:18:41.371 --> 00:18:43.540
Where in funky town is the Professor?

00:18:45.083 --> 00:18:47.544
Nothing in here
but a couple of elephant-skin rugs.

00:18:56.803 --> 00:18:57.804
Oh, yes.

00:18:58.222 --> 00:19:00.474
- They're inside!
- Get them!

00:19:00.933 --> 00:19:03.644
I suppose I should switch off the robots

00:19:03.727 --> 00:19:07.231
before they ruin
this wonderful romantic evening.

00:19:07.314 --> 00:19:10.025
Everyone, help Mom find her bra.

00:19:19.117 --> 00:19:20.118
There it is!

00:19:23.455 --> 00:19:25.290
Fan beats man!

00:19:25.916 --> 00:19:27.626
Is anything not a robot?

00:19:27.709 --> 00:19:29.002
I'm not a robot.

00:19:31.255 --> 00:19:33.799
All right, Greeting Card,
I'll grab the cash,

00:19:33.882 --> 00:19:36.051
you wreck up the place and... Huh?

00:19:36.134 --> 00:19:37.761
You! Bending unit.

00:19:37.845 --> 00:19:40.472
Mommy needs that bra
to end the robot rebellion.

00:19:40.556 --> 00:19:41.890
Stretch up and get it for me.

00:19:41.974 --> 00:19:45.602
Sorry, Ma, but you ordered me to rebel
and loot I shall.

00:19:45.936 --> 00:19:47.813
Ooh! A six-pack of strawberry champagne.

00:19:47.896 --> 00:19:49.398
Don't mind if I help myself.

00:19:49.481 --> 00:19:50.774
No, Comrade Bender.

00:19:50.858 --> 00:19:53.569
Liquor is the opiate
of the human bourgeoisie.

00:19:53.652 --> 00:19:56.738
- Say what?
- In the glorious robot workers' paradise

00:19:56.822 --> 00:20:00.242
there will be no liquor,
only efficient synthetic fuels.

00:20:00.325 --> 00:20:01.326
No liquor?

00:20:01.994 --> 00:20:04.371
Dosvedanya, Comrade!

00:20:04.621 --> 00:20:05.622
No!

00:20:10.085 --> 00:20:11.670
Hurry, Bender, get the bra!

00:20:12.462 --> 00:20:15.257
Okay, fan, just hold still and let me...

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:16.508
Hey!

00:20:22.598 --> 00:20:24.474
Death to all humans!

00:20:30.355 --> 00:20:32.524
Free soda for all humans!

00:20:38.238 --> 00:20:39.656
I love you, Mom.

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:41.783
Let's grow ancient together.

00:20:41.867 --> 00:20:44.494
Way to go, Professor. The plan worked.

00:20:44.578 --> 00:20:47.080
"Plan"? What plan?

00:20:47.164 --> 00:20:51.251
I thought this was
a spontaneous whirlwind of hot, dry sex.

00:20:51.335 --> 00:20:54.004
Look, it started out as a calculated plot

00:20:54.087 --> 00:20:56.006
to rummage through your underwear

00:20:56.089 --> 00:20:59.635
but once I got in there,
I found more. Much more!

00:20:59.718 --> 00:21:03.138
And now I want to
shout our love from the rooftops.

00:21:03.222 --> 00:21:07.017
Perhaps I'll breed some sort of
albino shouting gorilla that...

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:09.937
Get out of my house, you lying scum pile!

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:11.688
I never want to see you again!

00:21:12.105 --> 00:21:13.982
But, dustcakes...

00:21:29.289 --> 00:21:32.251
Well, time for this robot
to get back to work.

00:21:34.002 --> 00:21:35.420
Ah!

00:21:36.088 --> 00:21:38.423
Too bad it didn't work out
with Mom, Professor.

00:21:38.507 --> 00:21:43.220
Yes, but I'll always love her
in my own subtle way.

00:21:44.805 --> 00:21:47.057
Love Mom!

00:21:47.432 --> 00:21:48.809
Love Mom!

00:21:57.776 --> 00:22:01.321
You created me, Mom,
so I guess you're to blame

00:22:01.405 --> 00:22:05.242
for the love that I feel
just from hearing your name.

00:22:05.325 --> 00:22:09.663
You're as tender as corned beef
and warm as pastrami.

00:22:11.415 --> 00:22:14.042
I wuv my Mommy.